  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d6d120ec87984dd08ab49e9d51a59edd, type: 3}
  m_Name: Mural4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::WakeTheWalls.Murals.MuralData
  referenceImageName: Mural4
  displayName: The Spirit of African Leadership
  location: Covered brick alcove facing the paved court
  physicalSizeMeters: {x: 5.4, y: 3.509}
  story: 'The Spirit of African Leadership, by Samuel Daddy Ishimwe and Masha Studio
    from Rwanda, painted in 2020.


    A large mask of curved, interlocking shapes
    in gold, blue and black watches over five leaders painted into dark landscapes
    and divided by lines of gold: Queen Nzinga, Mansa Musa, Thomas Sankara, Kwame
    Nkrumah and Winnie Madikizela-Mandela. Mixing modern portraits with traditional
    mask symbolism, the mural links ancestral wisdom to the hopes of future generations,
    and celebrates African leadership, innovation and cultural identity.


    Tap
    a face to light it up and hear who it is, or tap the gold lines to let the light
    connect them.'
  experiencePrefab: {fileID: 7913823731028150729, guid: 91c717cef988741e689d4515a3a1990f, type: 3}
  palette:
  - {r: 0.356, g: 0.337, b: 0.304, a: 1}
  - {r: 0.513, g: 0.444, b: 0.347, a: 1}
  - {r: 0.24, g: 0.219, b: 0.195, a: 1}
  - {r: 0.741, g: 0.594, b: 0.395, a: 1}
  - {r: 0.492, g: 0.529, b: 0.519, a: 1}
  - {r: 0.855, g: 0.758, b: 0.582, a: 1}
  ambience: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 63d6717184514e668e36c33215db9eab, type: 3}
  spots:
  - topic: portrait_crown
    title: Queen Nzinga
    text: She ruled the Ndongo and Matamba kingdoms in the 17th century, in what
      is now Angola. She is painted in royal regalia with a crown and necklace, after
      her best-known historical portrait.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b63ab0f29f0a645a3a021d5aa38c503c, type: 3}
  - topic: portrait_turban
    title: Mansa Musa
    text: Emperor of the Mali Empire in the 14th century, often called one of the
      wealthiest people in history. He is painted in white robes and a headdress,
      holding a golden staff.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: dde1de3e40faf4a6589460db9210dcf0, type: 3}
  - topic: portrait_beret
    title: Thomas Sankara
    text: Former President of Burkina Faso and a Pan-Africanist revolutionary, painted
      in his signature red beret and military uniform.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e6e6406cefceb470d84b5ebee1bbe379, type: 3}
  - topic: portrait_right
    title: Kwame Nkrumah
    text: The first Prime Minister and President of Ghana, and a leading figure in
      the Pan-African movement. He sits next to Sankara.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4300f02e0c385465fa54d9626c36911d, type: 3}
  - topic: portrait_cap
    title: Winnie Madikizela-Mandela
    text: South African anti-apartheid activist and politician, painted smiling in
      glasses, a headwrap and beaded jewellery.
    voice: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f4fe22880daf0434b92bc2ffbdeb4d4c, type: 3}
